# Material Security


> Material Security is a cloud workspace security platform for Google Workspace and Microsoft 365, focused on detection and response across email, accounts/identity, and sensitive data.


Key notes:
- Material connects via API (not a gateway) to help security teams detect and respond to threats inside the cloud workspace.
- Use the “Security & Trust” links below for security posture and legal agreements.


## Product overview


- [What Material is](https://material.security/product): Platform overview for cloud workspace security.
- [Email security](https://material.security/product/email): Protect against advanced email threats and automate phishing response.
- [File security](https://material.security/product/files): Protect file data from risky user sharing and automatically classify sensitive data. 
- [Account security](https://material.security/product/accounts): Detect and respond to account takeover and identity threats.
- [Deployment & security model](https://material.security/products/deployment-and-security): How deployment works and key security controls.
- [Use Cases](https://material.security/use-cases): Various threats and use case applications for deploying comprehensive workspace security.
- [Google Workspace security](https://material.security/providers/google-workspace): Unified security that protects Gmail, Google Drive, identity and configurations. 
- [Microsoft 365 security](https://material.security/providers/microsoft-365): Purpose-built protection from email threats, data sprawl and user behavior across Microsoft 365. 






